cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Hephaestus, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Hephaestus: an in-browser open-source engine and databases for the thermodynamics and phase diagrams of slags, molten salts, and alloys"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Michael E.
    family-names: Bustamante
    affiliation: "Odinzen LLC, Houston, TX, United States"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-9001-8151"
    email: michaelbusta@odinzen.io
  - given-names: Gabriel
    family-names: Bustamante
    affiliation: "Odinzen LLC, Houston, TX, United States"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-3269-024X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/odinzen/hephaestus-mqmqa-public"
url: "https://odinzen.github.io/hephaestus-mqmqa-public/"
license:
  - AGPL-3.0-only
  - CC-BY-SA-4.0
abstract: >-
  Hephaestus is a C engine with Python and WebAssembly front ends for the Modified
  Quasichemical Model in the Quadruplet Approximation (MQMQA) and the Compound Energy
  Formalism, with open databases for oxide slags, molten salts, and alloys. It reads and
  writes FactSage-style .dat, Thermo-Calc .tdb, unified .utdb, and XTDB files, computes
  equilibria and phase diagrams, and runs entirely in the browser. The engine is licensed
  AGPL-3.0-only and the databases CC BY-SA 4.0.
keywords:
  - CALPHAD
  - MQMQA
  - modified quasichemical model
  - slag
  - molten salt
  - phase diagram
  - thermodynamics
